«
@@ ============================================================
@@ GCPoint — intermediate point on the great circle between two
@@ points of a sphere, at a given fraction of the route.
@@ Ed Williams, Aviation Formulary V1.47, "Intermediate points on a
@@ great circle".
@@
@@ Input : φ1 λ1 φ2 λ2 f — departure and destination (East
@@         positive), and the fraction of the route, 0 at departure,
@@         1 at destination. Plain numbers are degrees; angles with a
@@         unit are accepted.
@@ Output: φ λ — latitude and longitude of the point.
@@ Not defined for antipodal points, where every great circle through
@@ both is a shortest route.
@@ Angle mode and angle units setting are restored before returning.
@@ ============================================================

  → frac
  «
    4 →LIST
    « IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_r CONVERT UVAL ELSE Ⓒπ →Num * 180 / END »
    MAP LIST→ DROP frac
  »
  'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
  RAD NoAngleUnits
  → p1 q1 p2 q2 frac amode aunits
  «
    '2*ASIN(√(SIN((p2-p1)/2)²+COS(p1)*COS(p2)*SIN((q2-q1)/2)²))' EVAL
    → d12
    «
      'SIN((1-frac)*d12)/SIN(d12)' EVAL 'SIN(frac*d12)/SIN(d12)' EVAL
      → wa wb
      «
        'wa*COS(p1)*COS(q1)+wb*COS(p2)*COS(q2)' EVAL
        'wa*COS(p1)*SIN(q1)+wb*COS(p2)*SIN(q2)' EVAL
        'wa*SIN(p1)+wb*SIN(p2)' EVAL
        → xx yy zz
        «
          '(zz)∠(√(xx²+yy²))' EVAL 180 * Ⓒπ →Num / 1_° *
          '(yy)∠(xx)' EVAL 180 * Ⓒπ →Num / 1_° *
        »
      »
    »
    amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
  »
»
